---The MiniMenu is the primary mechanism for interacting with the game.
---
---Each element in the game, whether a 2D Interface Component or a 3D game world NPC Entity, will add MiniMenuEntries to
---the MiniMenu when the cursor, or a tap, is positioned over them. These entries are recalculated on every Client Logic
---tick, so long as the MiniMenu remains closed.
---
---When the MiniMenu is opened, by right-click or long-press, the current list of available entries is shown. The list
---is sorted by priority, with the higher priority entries shown at the top.
---
---Info: When accessing the MiniMenu via the API, higher priority entries are instead at the end of the list.
---
---The highest priority entry in the list is activated when you left-click or tap while the MiniMenu is closed. This is
---also the entry which interface tooltips are generated for, and which affects the current Cursor sprite.
---
---Accessing the MiniMenu: As the MiniMenu's list of MiniMenuEntries is in constant flux, access and making changes to
---the MiniMenu is restricted to within specific Events.
---
---The principal event for managing the MiniMenu is Event.MiniMenuReady. This event provides access to the full list of
---entries, as well as the ability to Swap entries.
---
---Additional events Event.MiniMenuOpened and Event.MiniMenuClosed provide read-only access to the presented list of
---entries.
---
---Event.MiniMenuEntryAdded is called when each new entry is added, providing access only to that entry.
---
---Event.MiniMenuEntrySelected is called when a MiniMenu entry is chosen. This can be from a left-click or tap on a game
---element, or from selecting an entry from the open MiniMenu.
---
---The only MiniMenu state available outside of these events is MiniMenu.IsOpen().
---
---MiniMenuEntry: A MiniMenuEntry contains information about a specific action from a specific source, which should
---occur when the entry is selected.
---
---The entry source, like an NPC entity or Interface Component, is indicated by MiniMenuEntryType, which covers all the
---places where actions can be gathered.
---
---Entries also provide additional data, depending on the MiniMenuEntryType. This can be things like access to a source
---NPCEntity or a ground CoordGrid.
---
---See MiniMenuEntry properties for additional information.
---
---Actions and Ops: There is a fixed number of possible actions available, shown in MiniMenuActionType. These actions
---can be handled by the Client, sent to the Server, or both at the same time.
---
---The legacy name for these actions is called an Op. Each source, like an NPC or Component, has a set of numbered Ops
---which are individually referred to as Op1, Op2, etc.
---
---Each type also has a Target Op, referred to as OpT. This is used to apply one entity to another - such as a Spell or
---Ability to an in-game NPC.
---
---Verbs and Subjects: Most entries have a Verb, like "Chop down", and a Subject, like "Oak Tree". Some simpler entries
---have only a Verb, such as "Walk" or "Cancel".
---
---There are a few common verb types, shown in MiniMenuActionVerbType. These are used to present display strings for
---common Ops like `MiniMenuActionVerbType.ATTACK` or `MiniMenuActionVerbType.EXAMINE`, while
---`MiniMenuActionVerbType.OP` covers all custom Ops.
---
---Custom Ops are found in entity configs, or are manually defined in Component OP configs.
---
---For entities, the Subject display string comes from the entity config's `displayName` while the Verb string depends
---on each individual Op found in the entity config.
---
---Sorting: Entries are sorted within the MiniMenu in the following order:
---@class MiniMenu
---@field isOpen boolean (Read-only) Whether the MiniMenu is currently open.
---@field entryCount integer (Read-only) How many entries are in the MiniMenu.
---@field entries MiniMenuEntry[] (Read-only) A list of current entries available in the MiniMenu.
MiniMenu = {}

---Returns whether the MiniMenu is currently open. This static method be called at any time.
---@return boolean # Whether the MiniMenu is currently open.
function MiniMenu.IsOpen() end

---Adds a MiniMenuEntry to the end of the current list of minimenu entries. It will be displayed with the label
---specified and call the Lua function specified, with any additional arguments provided in order.
---
---Warning: This method is only available during Event.MiniMenuEntryAdded and Event.MiniMenuReady. When called during
---Event.MiniMenuEntryAdded the new entry will be added immediately after the current entry. When called during
---Event.MiniMenuReady the new entry will be added at the bottom of `MiniMenu.entries`.
---@param label string The text displayed for the entry in the minimenu.
---@param action function A Lua function that can take any number of arguments, including none.
---@param ... any A comma-separated list of arguments that will be passed to the function specified in the action parameter.
function MiniMenu:Add(label, action, ...) end

---Swaps MiniMenuEntries found at the two provided indices of `MiniMenu.entries`.
---
---Info: The index values are 1-based.
---
---Warning: This method is only available during Event.MiniMenuReady.
---@param indexA integer The index of the first MiniMenuEntry in `MiniMenu.entries`.
---@param indexB integer The index of the second MiniMenuEntry in `MiniMenu.entries`.
function MiniMenu:Swap(indexA, indexB) end

---@class MiniMenuEntry
---@field actionType MiniMenuActionType (Read-only) The action type of this entry.
---@field actionEntryType MiniMenuEntryType (Read-only) The entry source type of this entry.
---@field actionVerbType MiniMenuActionVerbType (Read-only) The verb type of this entry.
---@field verbText string (Read-only) The verb name of the entry.
---@field subjectText string (Read-only) The subject name of the entry.
---@field extraText string (Read-only) An additional string appended to the entry.
---@field fullText string (Read-only) The full text displayed when the entry is shown in the MiniMenu if `overrideText` has not been set. Combines `verbText`, `subjectText` and `extraText` in that order.
---@field overrideText string? (Writeable) Override text for an entry supplied by a plugin. This is displayed in place of an entry's `fullText` if set.
---@field cursorID integer (Read-only) The Cursor config ID shown when this entry is active. Use `config.Cursor.FromID(cursorID)` to obtain the config.
---@field iconSpriteIDs integer[] (Read-only) An array of sprite IDs which are drawn next to the entry text. Empty if none are drawn.
---@field subjectOnOtherLevel boolean (Read-only) Whether the source entity is on a different level from the Player Character. NOTE: Not always correct.
---@field subjectHash integer (Read-only) A (sort of) unique identifier for the entry. This identifier is only unique for entries that share the same `actionEntryType`.
---@field npcData NPCData? (Read-only) A collection of data related to this entry. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
---@field locData LocData? (Read-only) A collection of data related to this entry. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
---@field objData ObjData? (Read-only) A collection of data related to this entry. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
---@field playerData PlayerData? (Read-only) A collection of data related to this entry. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
---@field groundData GroundData? (Read-only) A collection of data related to this entry. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
---@field mapElementData MapElementData? (Read-only) A collection of data related to this entry. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
---@field componentData ComponentData? (Read-only) A collection of data related to this entry. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
local MiniMenuEntry = {}

---@class NPCData
---@field entity NPCEntity (Read-only) The NPC entity source for this entry.
local NPCData = {}

---@class LocData
---@field coordGridX integer (Read-only) The south-west tile X coordinate the Loc entity is positioned at.
---@field coordGridZ integer (Read-only) The south-west tile Z coordinate the Loc entity is positioned at.
---@field config LocType (Read-only) The config for the Loc entity.
local LocData = {}

---@class ObjData
---@field entity ObjStackEntity (Read-only) The ObjStack entity source for this entry.
---@field stackIndex integer (Read-only) The specific object within the source ObjStackEntity that this MiniMenuEntry relates to. Use this with ObjStackEntity:GetEntry().
---@field config ObjType (Read-only) The config for the specific object that this MiniMenuEntry relates to.
local ObjData = {}

---@class PlayerData
---@field entity PlayerEntity (Read-only) The Player entity source for this entry.
local PlayerData = {}

---@class GroundData
---@field coordGridX integer (Read-only) The tile X coordinate this entry is focused at.
---@field coordGridZ integer (Read-only) The tile Z coordinate this entry is focused at.
---@field fromMiniMap boolean (Read-only) `true` if this entry was created from the MiniMap. `false` if this entry was created from the 3D world view.
local GroundData = {}

---@class MapElementData
---@field mapElementID integer (Read-only) The MapElement config ID shown when this entry is active. Use `config.MapElement.FromID(mapElementID)` to obtain the config. TODO: `MapElement` configs are not available yet.
---@field categoryID integer (Read-only) The Category ID belonging to this map element.
local MapElementData = {}

---@class ComponentData
---@field opIndex integer (Read-only) The op index for this entry. Valid values are `1` -> `10`.
---@field objConfig ObjType? (Read-only) Some Components allow ObjType IDs to be assigned to them, such as Sprites and Models. This property provides the config, if set on the source Component. Will be `nil` if unavailable.
---@field component ui.Component (Read-only) The Component source for this entry.
local ComponentData = {}

---A list of all the possible source types for each MiniMenuEntry.
---@enum MiniMenuEntryType
MiniMenuEntryType = {
    NONE = 0,
    INTERFACE = 1,
    OBJ = 2,
    LOC = 3,
    NPC = 4,
    OTHER = 5,
    MINIMENU = 6,
    PLAYER = 7,
    SELF = 8,
    MAP = 9,
    PLUGIN = 10,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `MiniMenuEntryType.FromID(MiniMenuEntryType.NONE)` is `"NONE"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function MiniMenuEntryType.FromID(value) end

---The type of action for each entry. `MiniMenuActionVerbType.OP` is the most common.
---@enum MiniMenuActionVerbType
MiniMenuActionVerbType = {
    ATTACK = 0,
    EXAMINE = 1,
    OP = 2,
    UNSPECIFIED = 3,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `MiniMenuActionVerbType.FromID(MiniMenuActionVerbType.ATTACK)` is `"ATTACK"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function MiniMenuActionVerbType.FromID(value) end

